      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] This check is mathematically impossible to trigger and constitutes dead code.\n\nOn line 623, `validate_fp_buffer_offset(current_frame_size, offset, size)` ensures that `offset + size \u003c\u003d current_frame_size` (and it uses `check_add_overflow` internally to prevent integer wrap-around).\nSince `current_frame_size` is explicitly bounded by `sizeof(fp_buffer)` on line 619, we are mathematically guaranteed that `offset \u003c\u003d sizeof(fp_buffer)` upon reaching this block.\n\nBecause `offset` cannot exceed `sizeof(fp_buffer)` (which is a relatively small constant), the addition `offset + FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_OFFSET` can never wrap around `UINT32_MAX`.\n\nThe regression test added in this CL (`test_get_frame_shifted_integer_overflow`) actually passes because `validate_fp_buffer_offset` correctly catches the large `offset` parameter and returns an error *before* execution ever reaches this new check. I recommend dropping this redundant check.",
