      "message": "Let\u0027s keep the test. However, review this Gemini feedback for correctness:\n\n---\n\nIn your final assertion, you reference `expected_canary`:\n\n```c\nzassert_mem_equal(output_buffer, expected_canary, sizeof(output_buffer), ...);\n\n```\n\nHowever, `expected_canary` is not defined in the scope of this test. Since you initialized the buffer with `0xA5`, you need an array filled with `0xA5` to compare it against.\n\nYou can fix this easily by defining the expected state at the top of the test:\n\n```c\nZTEST(fpsensor_get_frame, test_get_frame_shifted_integer_overflow)\n{\n\tuint8_t output_buffer[kMaxReadSize];\n\tuint8_t expected_canary[kMaxReadSize];\n\t\n\t/* Initialize both with our known canary value */\n\tmemset(output_buffer, 0xA5, sizeof(output_buffer));\n\tmemset(expected_canary, 0xA5, sizeof(expected_canary));\n\n\tglobal_context.current_capture_type \u003d FP_CAPTURE_SIMPLE_IMAGE;\n        \n        // ... rest of your test ...\n\n```",
